 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-007\", \"clauses\": {\"compose\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F10\", \"template\": \"{question}\", \"reasoning\": \"F10 draws rows of the _ITEM_POOL bank. The row with answer rectangle and question about two identical squares placed side by side is a compose task that is correct for every reading of the question.\"}, \"decompose\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F10\", \"template\": \"{question}\", \"reasoning\": \"The row about a rectangle cut into two equal pieces down the middle, and the row about a square cut on a slant from corner to corner, are decompose tasks. Both are read through F10.\"}, \"triangles\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F10\", \"template\": \"{question}\", \"reasoning\": \"The row about a square cut on a slant produces two triangles as the keyed answer, so F10 addresses the triangles object.\"}, \"squares\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F10\", \"template\": \"{question}\", \"reasoning\": \"The row about two identical squares placed side by side uses squares as the objects being composed.\"}, \"rectangles\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F10\", \"template\": \"{question}\", \"reasoning\": \"The rows about two identical squares forming a rectangle and a long rectangle cut across its width into two equal squares address the rectangles object.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F08\", \"F10\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"{answer}\", \"{question}\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"Two rows of the _ITEM_POOL bank, which is one_row_per_problem true, are wrong for a learner. Row 1 has question text about two triangles placed together matching their longest straight edges, with keyed answer rectangle. The question does not say the triangles are right triangles. Two congruent triangles joined along a side in general form a parallelogram, not a rectangle, so the keyed answer through F08 {answer} and the question through F10 {question} can mislead. Row 5 has question text about two identical triangles joined along matching straight edges to make a 4-sided shape with equal sides, with keyed answer square. Equal sides alone also fits a rhombus, and the distractors do not exclude it, so the key through F08 {answer} and the question through F10 {question} are not determined by the text. Rows with answers two rectangles, two triangles, rectangle (two identical squares) and two squares are correct as written, and the hint families F01 to F04 and the vocabulary use of sides through the gated word sides are within the gate. The word width in row 6 is not gated, so it is not a failing finding. F05 and F07 print only generator choices and are not themselves faulty. Because the same keyed answers also reach F05 in correct_answer and format_data.options, the fault is in the bank rows, not in the wording of F05.\"}",
